{"items":[{"source_ids":["n1","n2"],"text":"# pi-identity
pi-identity provides scoped automatic attachment of living notebook notes and auditing. Following issue #612, commit 7a362d6, note headers support `paths:` and `touches:`. Path prefixes or globs scope automatic attachment when chats read, edit, grep, or run shell commands (including bash) against matching paths; touch triggers scope attachment when queued tasks start with matching touches. Configure scopes with `notebook(action="edit", id="<id>", paths=[...], touches=[...])`.

`notebook(action="audit")` checks note integrity. Reported issues can include dead disk or file paths, lines longer than 240 characters, empty `##` sections, and leftover `(n...)` or `(d...)` references. The clean result is `Audit OK: 0 issues`."}],"ejected":[]}

